DriveHierarchy Dataset License and Third-Party Notices
======================================================

Primary dataset license: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike
4.0 International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

This primary license is consistent with the corresponding OpenReview
submission. Third-party components and derived material remain subject to the
exceptions and source terms identified below.

1. Primary license for DriveHierarchy-authored data
---------------------------------------------------

To the extent that the DriveHierarchy authors own the relevant rights, original
benchmark annotations, documentation, and closed-loop scenario descriptions are
made available under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike
4.0 International license:

This grant does not cover third-party data, annotations derived from third-party
datasets, third-party software, simulator assets, trademarks, or any material
for which the DriveHierarchy authors do not have authority to grant a license.

2. DriveHierarchy-authored code
-------------------------------

Source code written by the DriveHierarchy authors is made available under the
Apache License 2.0, unless a file or directory states otherwise. The complete
Apache License 2.0 text appears below.

3. Third-party and derived components
-------------------------------------

Third-party material and annotations derived from third-party datasets are not
relicensed by DriveHierarchy. The original terms continue to apply and prevail
over this notice:

* nuScenes and nuPlan material, including derived data:
  Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 together with the
  Motional Dataset Terms:
  https://www.nuscenes.org/terms-of-use

* NAVSIM: repository code and assets are Apache-2.0 unless otherwise stated;
  its datasets, including nuPlan and OpenScene, retain their own distribution
  licenses:
  https://github.com/autonomousvision/navsim

* Wayve LingoQA-derived material (including
  Open_Loop_Evaluation/R1_4_Situation_Description.jsonl): governed by the Wayve
  Dataset Licence Agreement for Non-Commercial Use. That agreement is
  non-transferable and non-sublicensable:
  https://github.com/wayveai/LingoQA/blob/main/LICENCE

  Required attribution from that agreement:
  "This work was made using the Wayve LingoQA dataset and benchmark, provided
  by Wayve Technologies Ltd under licence terms available at
  https://github.com/wayveai/LingoQA."

* Honda Research Institute DRAMA-derived material (including
  Open_Loop_Evaluation/R1_3_Location_Questions.jsonl): the source dataset is
  available to university-affiliated researchers for non-commercial use:
  https://usa.honda-ri.com/drama

  The public DRAMA page does not state a general redistribution license.
  DriveHierarchy does not grant redistribution rights to the underlying DRAMA
  material. Redistributors must obtain any permission required from its owner.

* CARLA 0.9.13: CARLA-specific code is MIT-licensed, CARLA-specific assets are
  CC-BY-licensed, Unreal Engine 4 has separate terms, and bundled dependencies
  may have additional licenses:
  https://github.com/carla-simulator/carla/tree/0.9.13

* Eclipse SUMO is an external dependency. SUMO-originated code or data, if
  present, remains under EPL-2.0 with GPL-2.0-or-later as a secondary license,
  except where separately identified:
  https://eclipse.dev/sumo/docs/Downloads.html

* WOMD-Reasoning-derived material (including
  Open_Loop_Evaluation/R3_3_MultiAgent_Intent.jsonl): the language annotations
  are governed by the WOMD-Reasoning license from the Regents of the University
  of California, which permits educational, research, and not-for-profit use
  and provides separate limited commercial permissions:
  https://github.com/yhli123/WOMD-Reasoning/blob/main/LICENSE

  WOMD-Reasoning is built on the Waymo Open Motion Dataset. The Waymo Dataset
  License Agreement for Non-Commercial Use also applies, including its
  attribution and sharing requirements:
  https://waymo.com/open/terms/

Other third-party sources identified in dataset metadata remain governed by
their respective source licenses. Provenance metadata is informational and does
not itself grant or replace any license.

4. No additional rights
-----------------------

Nothing in this file grants rights that the DriveHierarchy authors do not own
or have authority to license. Users and redistributors are responsible for
complying with all applicable source terms, attribution requirements, and
non-commercial-use restrictions.

5. Disclaimer
-------------

THE MATERIAL IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR
A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.

6. Safety and scope notice
--------------------------

DriveHierarchy is a research benchmark and has not been validated for
real-world vehicle deployment, safety certification, regulatory approval, or
direct control of a vehicle. Benchmark scores, including closed-loop simulator
scores, are not calibrated measures of crash risk and must not be represented
as evidence of deployment readiness. This notice describes the validated scope
of the release and does not replace or modify the license terms above.

